// 010.13 (D36, #46, #50, #61): `Function` application `f(k)`, `Count(pred)`, `Amount name Is expr`,
// `Decided by ... At least n/d`, `Bool` without `()`, multi-name powers, and single-party duties.
Fact member Identified by Alice, Bob, Carol
Fact asset Identified by Flat, Boat
Fact usd Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Bool active
Function worth Identified by asset * usd
Function owner Identified by asset * member
Fact marital Identified by asset
Fact present Identified by member
Function weight Identified by member * int
Fact yes-vote Identified by member

Amount marital-pool Is Sum(Foreach asset: worth(asset) When marital(asset))

Power pay, transfer Actor member Related to usd
  Valid when active && usd <= marital-pool

Duty keep-minutes Holder member

Power adopt-budget Actor member
  Decided by member Weighted by weight At least 2/3 In yes-vote
.
+active.
?active.
+worth(Flat, 30000). +worth(Boat, 10000).
+marital(Flat).
+owner(Boat, Bob).
?(worth(Flat) == 30000).
?(owner(Boat) == Bob).
?(marital-pool == 30000).
?valid pay(Alice, 20000).
?valid transfer(Alice, 20000).
?!valid pay(Alice, 40000).

+present(Alice). +present(Carol).
?(Count(present) == 2).

+keep-minutes(Alice).
?keep-minutes(Alice).

+weight(Alice, 50). +weight(Bob, 30). +weight(Carol, 20).
+yes-vote(Alice).
?!valid adopt-budget(Alice).
+yes-vote(Bob).
?valid adopt-budget(Alice).
